WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.030
I joined our pupils table to the marks,

2
00:00:03.490 --> 00:00:04.990
and sent the report to the head.

3
00:00:05.530 --> 00:00:07.290
Two pupils had vanished from it.

4
00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:10.120
Nobody noticed for a whole term.

5
00:00:11.370 --> 00:00:13.790
Today: joining tables, and reports

6
00:00:13.790 --> 00:00:15.670
that show only what's needed.

7
00:00:16.930 --> 00:00:18.930
A join puts rows from two

8
00:00:18.930 --> 00:00:20.290
tables side by side.

9
00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:24.020
JOIN names the second table, and ON

10
00:00:24.020 --> 00:00:27.120
says how rows match: the mark's pupil

11
00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:29.220
number equals the pupil's id.

12
00:00:30.450 --> 00:00:33.190
A plain JOIN is an inner join: it

13
00:00:33.190 --> 00:00:34.910
keeps only rows that match.

14
00:00:35.650 --> 00:00:37.850
A pupil with no mark simply

15
00:00:37.850 --> 00:00:39.830
vanishes, without a word.

16
00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:42.960
LEFT JOIN keeps every row of the first

17
00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:45.200
table, and fills the gaps with NULL.

18
00:00:46.340 --> 00:00:48.500
So, to find the pupils with no

19
00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:51.580
mark, use a left join and keep the

20
00:00:51.580 --> 00:00:53.400
rows where the mark is NULL.

21
00:00:53.950 --> 00:00:56.170
That's the list of who missed the test.

22
00:00:57.450 --> 00:00:59.310
Joins can multiply rows too.

23
00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:02.560
A pupil who sat the test and a resit

24
00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:05.000
appears twice, once per mark.

25
00:01:05.650 --> 00:01:08.730
So count before and after: are rows

26
00:01:08.730 --> 00:01:10.790
missing, or counted twice?

27
00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:12.510
Quick check!

28
00:01:13.150 --> 00:01:16.990
I do an inner join of pupils and marks.

29
00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:20.290
What happens to a pupil who has no mark?

30
00:01:21.590 --> 00:01:23.490
They're left out, silently.

31
00:01:24.390 --> 00:01:26.550
That's how my two pupils vanished.

32
00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:28.880
When every pupil must

33
00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:30.940
appear, use a left join.

34
00:01:32.220 --> 00:01:34.940
Now think about who reads the report.

35
00:01:35.670 --> 00:01:38.250
A parent needs their own child's marks.

36
00:01:38.980 --> 00:01:41.660
The head needs averages per class.

37
00:01:42.450 --> 00:01:44.710
Nobody needs phone numbers and

38
00:01:44.710 --> 00:01:46.730
health notes in a marks report.

39
00:01:48.050 --> 00:01:50.450
So select only the columns each

40
00:01:50.450 --> 00:01:52.730
reader needs, and only their rows.

41
00:01:53.490 --> 00:01:56.310
A join can bring in everything; a good

42
00:01:56.310 --> 00:01:58.450
report query leaves most of it out.

43
00:01:59.690 --> 00:02:01.790
In the app, try each join

44
00:02:01.790 --> 00:02:03.170
of pupils and marks.

45
00:02:03.940 --> 00:02:06.280
Watch who disappears, who appears

46
00:02:06.280 --> 00:02:09.180
twice, and how the count of rows and

47
00:02:09.180 --> 00:02:10.840
the count of marks drift apart.

48
00:02:12.190 --> 00:02:12.710
Your turn.

49
00:02:13.340 --> 00:02:15.100
A report for parents' evening

50
00:02:15.100 --> 00:02:16.420
goes to each family.

51
00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:19.070
Which columns should it show?

52
00:02:20.290 --> 00:02:22.410
Just the child's name and their own

53
00:02:22.410 --> 00:02:24.410
marks, for that family only.

54
00:02:25.020 --> 00:02:28.360
Remember: a join matches rows on a key.

55
00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:31.100
Inner joins drop what doesn't match;

56
00:02:31.560 --> 00:02:33.240
left joins keep it as NULL.

57
00:02:33.800 --> 00:02:35.920
And a report shows only

58
00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:37.100
what its reader needs.

59
00:02:38.480 --> 00:02:41.100
Try it in class tomorrow: ask your

60
00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:43.860
pupils what a parent, the school

61
00:02:43.860 --> 00:02:46.960
nurse and the head teacher each need

62
00:02:46.960 --> 00:02:48.060
from the school records.

63
00:02:48.870 --> 00:02:51.830
They sort column cards into three piles.

64
00:02:52.650 --> 00:02:55.490
Which columns does nobody need at all?
